{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #892: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Is there a necessary and sufficient condition for a sequence of integers $b_1<b_2<\\cdots$ that ensures there exists a primitive sequence $a_1<a_2<\\cdots$ (i.e. no element divides another) with $a_n \\ll b_n$ for all $n$?\n\nIn particular, is this always possible if there are no non-trivial solutions to $(b_i,b_j)=b_k$? Current best: It is known that\\[\\sum \\frac{1}{b_n\\log b_n}<\\infty\\]and\\[\\sum_{b_n<x}\\frac{1}{b_n} =o\\left(\\frac{\\log x}{\\sqrt{\\log\\log x}}\\right)\\]are both necessary. Prize: no. Tags: number theory, primitive sets."},"claim_id":"vcl_5340c62ec37bedb94da03bd2636c755902b89b7c7555e0d737c8b159d8a9edc2","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:892","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_263038e7cc4c8bee","object_root":"sha256:f7c0e15440b1336255d9d2031173c54736467adb9a53b7b7a0c241e6c980fc54","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","